WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/StatusPageSkeleton.tsx — a PURE presentational skeleton (named
  export `StatusPageSkeleton`), shown during the System-Status page's initial fetch so there is no layout shift
  once data loads. It imports only GlassPanel (@/components/ui) + Skeleton (@/components/feedback) and renders the
  web root `space-y-5 max-w-3xl mx-auto` with role="status" / aria-busy="true" / aria-label="Loading system
  status" / data-testid="status-page-skeleton". Six logical regions = nine direct children (pixel/percent sizes
  map 1 px = 1 pt, 1 % = 0.01):
    1. Hero        GlassPanel.p-5 → flex items-start gap-4: avatar 56×56 rounded ; [60%×24 ; 40%×14] ; 120×36
    2. Chip bar    flex gap-2 overflow-hidden: 8× Skeleton 92×32 rounded-full (shrink-0)
    3. Health      GlassPanel.p-3 space-y-1: header 80×18 (mb-2) ; 6× SkeletonRow (w-full ×44)
    4. Action items GlassPanel.p-4 space-y-2: title 180×18 ; 2× SkeletonRow height 32 (w-full)
    5. Resources   GlassPanel.p-4 space-y-3: title 120×18 ; 5× SkeletonRow height 28 (w-full)
    6. Accordions  4× GlassPanel.p-5 → flex items-center gap-3: icon 20×20 ; [40%×16 ; 60%×12 mt-1] ; badge 60×24
  Data sources: NONE (prompt records "(none — pure presentational component)"). No t() calls — the surface is
  anonymous. No loading/empty/error/stale/offline branches exist in the source: the skeleton IS the loading
  affordance; the parent System-Status surface swaps it out for content/empty/error once its query resolves.
  Reproduced 1:1 (covenant pt 2). The one native-only string is the VoiceOver busy label the Apple HIG
  loading-state contract requires (the web `aria-label`, localized).

