PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  GlassPanel              → TSGlassPanel (Sources/Components/UI/Cards.swift) — system material + glass border.
  Skeleton                → TSSkeleton (Sources/Components/Feedback/Skeletons.swift) — shimmer that respects Reduce
                            Motion (accessibilityReduceMotion). web w-full → width:nil; web "{n}px" → points; web
                            "{n}%" → GeometryReader fraction; web rounded-full → cornerRadius = height/2 (circle on
                            the square avatar, capsule on the wide chips); web mt-* → topInset.
  space-y-5/gap-*/p-*/mb-2 → TSSpacing tokens (xl=20 space-y-5 · lg=16 gap-4 · md=12 gap-3/space-y-3 · sm=8
                            gap-2/space-y-2/mb-2 · xs=4 space-y-1) — exact token rhythm, not ported px.
  max-w-3xl mx-auto       → .frame(maxWidth: 768).frame(maxWidth: .infinity) — capped reading width, centered.
  overflow-hidden (chips) → HStack(...).clipped() — the chip row is clipped on compact width as in the source.
  i18n                    : zero English literals in code; the one VoiceOver label resolves via SPSStrings
                            (NSLocalizedString, table "StatusPageSkeleton") with the English value in .strings.
  a11y                    : whole surface is ONE VoiceOver element (.accessibilityElement(children:.ignore) +
                            label + .updatesFrequently, mirroring role="status"/aria-busy); decorative shimmer
                            blocks are .accessibilityHidden (in TSSkeleton). accessibilityIdentifier mirrors the
                            web data-testid for UI tests. No interactive elements exist in the source, so none to
                            label.
  telemetry               : view.opened surface="StatusPageSkeleton" via StatusPageSkeletonSurface.reportOpen
                            (P1/S11), default OSLog sink; previews use a no-op sink.
  states                  : the surface is itself the LOADING affordance; empty/error/stale/offline belong to the
                            parent (web Data sources = none). Documented, reproduced 1:1 — no scope narrowing.

